#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:61
msgid "Cache status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:62
msgid "Read the state of Simple Redis Cache on this site: whether Redis is reachable, whether the object cache and the full-page HTML cache are enabled and their drop-ins installed, the page cache lifetime, which content changes clear cached pages automatically, the Cloudflare purge settings, outage markers and the background removal of old cache generations. Redis memory and hit/miss numbers describe the whole Redis server, which other sites may share. Read-only: call it before clearing anything, or to find out why a change is not visible to visitors yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:76
msgid "Clear cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:77
msgid "Clear a whole cache layer of Simple Redis Cache on this site. scope \"page\" clears every cached HTML page (and the Cloudflare zone when the site enabled that for clearing the page cache); \"object\" clears the Redis object cache and also deletes every standard WordPress transient from the database, including transients of other plugins; \"all\" does both, like the \"Clear all cache\" button. Clearing is instant, but the next visits are slower until the cache fills again. Usually not needed after editing content through WordPress: the site clears changed pages itself when it is set up to (see simple-redis-cache-status), and simple-redis-cache-flush-post clears one post. Needs the manage_options capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:85
msgid "What to clear: \"page\" (HTML pages), \"object\" (object cache and database transients) or \"all\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:104
msgid "Clear a post’s cached page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:105
msgid "Clear the cached HTML of one published post or page and of its translations, so visitors get the current version; with related set to true, also the archives of its categories, tags and other public terms and the listing pages (home page, blog page, archives, search). The same addresses are purged at Cloudflare when the site enabled Cloudflare purging on post updates. Works only when the site uses per-post invalidation (page_cache.invalidation in simple-redis-cache-status); otherwise it returns an error, and simple-redis-cache-flush with scope \"page\" clears all pages instead. Needs the right to edit that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:113
msgid "ID of the post, page or other public entry whose cached page to clear."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-abilities.php:118
msgid "Also clear its term archives and the listing pages. Default false."
msgstr ""

