#: includes/class-simple-redis-cache-github-updater.php:103
msgid "Version 0.10.0 gives AI agents (Simple MCP, the WordPress MCP Adapter) tools to read the cache status and clear the cache, removes keys of old cache generations from Redis in the background, batches object-cache reads and writes, invalidates pages after post meta changes and removed terms, keeps pages that print a nonce only while it is valid, and requires a signed token for the warming header. Version 0.9.0 can clear the whole cache when content changes: the whole HTML page cache, or the page and the object cache together, and the whole Cloudflare zone, once per request after published content, its terms or the site change. Version 0.8.0 fixes the findings of a code review: changes lost during a Redis outage no longer come back afterwards, a stalled Redis is skipped for 15 seconds, the home page, archives, search and 404 pages are invalidated when content is published, menus, widgets, the theme and updates clear the page cache, 404 and search pages live at most 10 minutes, stored pages are compressed and signed, a copied site gets its own cache namespace, and updates are pinned to one commit."
